From ad3685697cc34842d590e82f2242cb2f30bd2452 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:05:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] chat: make the turnStarted reducer case idempotent

A client that applies chat/turnStarted optimistically and replays it over
confirmed state (the write-ahead reconciliation model) had its streamed
content wiped on every replay, because the reducer rebuilt activeTurn with
an empty responseParts array regardless of what the state already held.

ChatTurnStarted now returns the state unchanged when its turnId is already
the active turn, or already appears in the completed turns, so a replayed
start never resets a turn in progress and never resurrects a finished turn
as an empty active one. Restarting a finished turn remains the job of
chat/turnResume.

Fixtures cover both no-op branches. The Go, Kotlin, Swift, and .NET reducers
still need the matching guard before the new fixtures pass there.
